  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Recovery Action Plan (JRAP) - Western Nepal Earthquake</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to the National Emergency Operations Centre, 62,000 homes were affected (35,455 partially damaged and 26,557 completely damaged) by the earthquake which struck Jajarkot district in Karnali province in November 2023. To address the temporary shelter needs of affected families by three earthquakes of Jajarkot, Bajura and Doti, the Government of Nepal endorsed the Temporary Housing Construction Procedure for Earthquake Affected Households and pledged 1.41 billion Nepalese rupees to support reconstruction and recovery efforts. Through this project, the International Organization for Migration is supporting the Government of Nepal in creating an enabling environment for the long-term recovery and reconstruction of earthquake-affected communities. The project is contributing towards the empowerment of affected populations and those in vulnerable situations to become agents of their own recovery through rebuilding their homes as well as reducing future disaster risks.</narrative>
  </description>
